KW  - Privacy-preserving RAG
KW  - Differential privacy
KW  - Tabular data synthesis
KW  - Embedding optimization
AB  - Inherent conflicts between privacy risks and retrieval accuracy hinder the effectiveness of Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) for tabular data. Standard row linearization leaks sensitive information while failing to capture relational dependencies. Existing privacy strategies are insufficient: privacy-enhanced Large Language Models training is computationally prohibitive, while inference-time filtering creates a trade-off between utility and protection. We propose PrivTabRAG, a novel framework that decouples privacy from retrieval by generating and querying Differentially Private (DP) synthetic data. To overcome the utility limitations of standard DP synthesis in RAG tasks, we introduce Retrieval-Augmented Table Generation (RATG) to align synthetic data with semantic embedding spaces, and Sequential Consistency Embedding (SCE) to optimize the retriever for synthetic distributions. Experiments demonstrate that PrivTabRAG achieves utility competitive with non-private baselines while reducing Membership Inference Attack (MIA) success rates from over 90% to near-random chance ( ∼ 50%). By adopting a ”generate once, query infinitely” paradigm, PrivTabRAG provides a scalable, query-agnostic privacy guarantee with minimal utility cost.
ER  - 

