AB  - Forecasting plays a crucial role in modern safety-critical applications, such as space operations. However, the increasing use of deep forecasting models introduces a new security risk of Trojan horse attacks, carried out by hiding a backdoor in training data or directly in model weights. Once implanted, the backdoor is activated by a specific trigger pattern at test time, causing the model to produce manipulated predictions. We focused on this issue in our Trojan Horse Hunt data science competition, where more than 200 teams faced the task of reconstructing triggers hidden in deep forecasting models for spacecraft telemetry. Here, we describe the novel task formulation, benchmark set, evaluation protocol, and best solutions from the competition. We further summarize key insights and research directions for trigger reconstruction in time series forecasting models. All materials are publicly available on the official competition webpage (www.kaggle.com/competitions/trojan-horse-hunt-in-space).
