AB  - bdd2pw is an open-source Node.js package that converts Behaviour-Driven Development (BDD) specifications written in Gherkin into compiling Playwright TypeScript test projects. It is, to the author’s knowledge, the first npm-distributed package targeting BDD-Gherkin → Page Object Model scaffolding via the Microsoft Playwright Model Context Protocol (MCP) server: bdd2pw drives a real browser session through the MCP, snapshots the accessibility tree, and emits Page Objects whose locators are grounded in the running application. A schema-constrained large-language-model fallback resolves ambiguous step mappings without authoring code; under pinned configuration (cached MCP DOM snapshot, fixed model version, temperature zero, response caching), generated Page Objects are byte-stable across re-runs. In a controlled single-scenario comparison (login feature, one experienced engineer), the package reduces hand-authored Page Object effort from approximately four hours to under three minutes; a multi-application empirical evaluation across 8 publicly available web applications (24 Gherkin scenarios) shows the deterministic layer alone produces compilable Playwright projects in approximately 4 s per application on average, while the governed Anthropic LLM fallback additionally closes 62 percent of unmatched steps at a mean cost of USD 0.026 per application (Section 4).
